WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.890
A nerve carries its
message along one path,

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.760
to one target, in milliseconds.

3
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.220
A hormone takes a different road.

4
00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:11.200
A gland releases it
straight into the blood.

5
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:14.850
The blood carries it to
almost every cell in the body.

6
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.850
Yet only a few kinds of cell respond.

7
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.540
So why does each hormone
affect only a few?

8
00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:25.850
In this mission, you'll compare the
body's two ways of sending messages:

9
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.880
fast nerves and slower hormones.

10
00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.650
Then you'll map the glands
that release hormones,

11
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.280
from the brain down to the pancreas.

12
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:39.810
Your mission: find out why each hormone
affects only a few of the cells it reaches.
